{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tsm0420/geo-growth-engine/pulls/15","id":4901100701,"node_id":"PR_kwDOVMrF8s8AAAABJCDcnQ","html_url":"https://github.com/tsm0420/geo-growth-engine/pull/15","diff_url":"https://github.com/tsm0420/geo-growth-engine/pull/15.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/tsm0420/geo-growth-engine/pull/15.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/tsm0420/geo-growth-engine/issues/15","number":15,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Preserve filename identity when inferring crawler URLs","user":{"login":"tsm0420","id":62269874,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyMjY5ODc0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62269874?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsm0420","html_url":"https://github.com/tsm0420","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsm0420/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsm0420/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsm0420/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsm0420/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsm0420/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsm0420/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsm0420/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsm0420/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tsm0420/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Summary\n\nReserved filename characters could become URL query/fragment/escape syntax, so matching Disallow rules falsely passed. Encode each actual filesystem segment before URL parsing. Convert only the host platform separator, preserving literal POSIX backslashes as filename data. Keep canonical coverage, index conventions, training policy and unmeasured deployment behavior separate.\n\n```text\n#notes.html -> /%23notes.html\n?notes.html -> /%3Fnotes.html\n%2Fnotes.html -> /%252Fnotes.html\nPOSIX blocked\\notes.html -> /blocked%5Cnotes.html\n```\n\nRelates to #10, TICKET-013 only. **Depends on unmerged #14**, transitively #13/#12/#11/#9; targets #14's branch.\n\n## Evidence\n\nReal CLI red/green regressions cover both search bots, reserved names, spaces/index paths, ordinary/root controls and canonical independence. Initial Spec P2 found the literal-backslash gap; test-first correction and both final independent reviews resolved it. Final Standards and Spec have no outstanding findings and each ran all seven safety tests. Full suite: 110 pass, zero skips; typecheck/build pass. Actual local OS is Darwin arm64; the POSIX filename test explicitly skips on Windows, where that literal filename is unavailable. No Windows device run is claimed.\n\nReviewed source `6ac457319e85e734407eae1f05cf56805c34f932` passed clean-source checks and 22 expected extracted-package outcomes. Package SHA-256 `a07478c2c02f0a84f980b2923e24a1d4ae8e6bedd0274e782db3cba5757ab10d`. Frozen YinThread inputs, 16/1/2 summary and 146/145/1 counts remain unchanged. Original receipts/runtime/inventory: `docs/verification/TICKET-013/`; initial/final separate reviews: `docs/reviews/TICKET-013/`.\n\nHead `9f2ea9ca3c07a69fc3ee36093e6322f56b1f686c` adds evidence/docs only after reviewed source. Exact-head CI succeeded for `9f2ea9ca3c07a69fc3ee36093e6322f56b1f686c`: [verify job](https://github.com/tsm0420/geo-growth-engine/actions/runs/39042831393/job/117425595268), observed through Code Review. Executable/CI inputs and every package file match the verified immutable source.\n\n## Merge Danger\n\nDoor: two-way. Blast radius: inferred local export URLs and filename finding IDs. Previously false search-access passes now fail for correctly encoded blocked paths. No deployment routing adapter, dependency, live crawl, merge, tag or release.","created_at":"2026-10-17T14:55:42Z","updated_at":"2026-10-17T14:56:47Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"ee6c73e35c488c951e9be3a3da42bc1074b4b9fb","assignees":[],"requested_review